P5.4 — reconnect / partial-loss drill, and a chunk-loss bug it found
specs/readiness-recovery-10-10/tasks.md P5.4

date (UTC): 2026-08-02
commit:     e7d18e8
setup:      real realtime-gateway with REALTIME_CHAOS_DROP_AFTER_CHUNKS=3, MAX_DROPS=2,
            real ml-inference behind it, scripts/chaos-realtime-reconnect.mjs as the client

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
RECONNECT: PASS

  connect #1 (fresh single-use ticket) -> 3 chunks -> DROPPED by chaos
  backoff 456ms (equal jitter)
  connect #2 (fresh single-use ticket) -> 3 chunks -> DROPPED by chaos
  backoff 267ms
  connect #3 (fresh single-use ticket) -> 6 chunks -> clean close

  RESULT sent=12/12 acked=12 drops=2 tickets=3

  The reconnect contract holds: a fresh single-use ticket per connect, equal-jitter backoff,
  buffer-and-resume from the right chunk index. The client is told the session survived.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PARTIAL LOSS: FAIL — half the recitation was acknowledged and never stored

  chunks on disk:  6 of 12
  present:         ws-0000 ws-0001 ws-0002 ws-0003 ws-0004 ws-0005
  missing:         ws-0006 .. ws-0011

  Sampled at +0s, +1s, +2s, +5s and +10s with the gateway STILL RUNNING: 6 every time. This is not
  a teardown artifact and it is not a race that settles — the chunks never arrive.

  The pattern is the tell. Connections 1 and 2 were killed mid-stream by chaos and BOTH stored
  their chunks. Connection 3 closed NORMALLY and stored none of its six.

  The chunks were ACCEPTED, not rejected. The client counts only `ack.accepted === true` and
  counted 12, so `forward_chunk` returned Ok for all of them and they entered the session's mpsc
  channel. The forwarding task then delivered six of them and logged nothing about the other six —
  no `ML service rejected`, no retry exhaustion, no backpressure counter.

  MECHANISM NOT YET CONFIRMED. lib.rs:1033 spawns the forwarding task detached and lib.rs:1180
  breaks the read loop on `Message::Close`, which is where to start — but "the handler returns
  before the task drains" is a hypothesis that does not by itself explain why the two ABORTED
  connections drained and the cleanly-closed one did not. The next step is a run with tracing on
  the forward path, not another guess.

  ── on the reliability of this measurement ──
  Three runs said 6/12, 6/12, then 0/12. The 0/12 was a HARNESS ARTIFACT: the gateway had panicked
  at startup (ALLOW_INSECURE_DEFAULTS combined with METRICS_DEV_OPEN is refused) and the client had
  connected to a stale gateway from the previous run, still holding the port and forwarding into a
  deleted directory.

  The run recorded above was therefore re-done on unique ports (8431/8492) with an assertion that a
  gateway OF THIS RUN is listening before any measurement is taken. It reports 6/12 with the same
  missing set. The finding survived the check; it is recorded here because a number that moves
  between runs is worth nothing until you know why, and the first two runs happened to be right for
  reasons I had not verified.

WHY THIS MATTERS MORE THAN A DROPPED PACKET

  The gateway ACKed all 12. The client has no way to know. The session then finalizes,
  transcription reads storage, and the aligner scores SIX chunks of audio against the FULL
  canonical passage — so every word the learner did recite, in the half that was lost, is recorded
  as a word they missed.

  That is a false judgement about how a person recited the Quran, produced silently, with an audit
  trail that says the recording was delivered. It is the exact failure the review gates exist to
  prevent, arriving underneath them.

  It also confirms the standing audit finding that gateway acknowledgements mean "queued", not
  "stored" — measured here rather than inferred.

NOT FIXED IN THIS RUN, deliberately. A drain fix on a detached task is the kind of concurrency
change that goes wrong when rushed at the end of a session. The reproduction is deterministic and
takes 20 seconds, so the fix can be written against a red test rather than against a hypothesis.

STILL NOT RUN for P5.4: long-audio, timeout, duplicate-delivery, recovery.
